{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789391170,"nonce":"hZN48JUippEBpdYvoxDnE2ugQ6A=","title":"Compiled code calls the runtime for every object allocation","message":"Every `New` of an HOBJ in LLVM-compiled code called `hlp_alloc_obj_sized`,\nwhose fast path is the thread's bump region behind a `thread_local!`: on\nMach-O that access is a `_tlv_get_addr` call per allocation, on Linux a\n`fs`-relative load plus the function call itself. binary_trees allocates\n28M objects (900MB); the profile on the NUC had the allocation fast path,\nthe region refill and the block zeroing at about a third of the run, the\nGC pause at a fifth, and the program's own code at 14%.\n\nwren_lift's tiers inline the Immix bump into JIT code, which is the\nobvious lever; what stopped ash doing it is thread identity: the region\nis per thread, the same compiled function runs on any thread, and\ncompiled code has no thread register.\n\nFix: the runtime tells the JIT how to reach the running thread's `Tlab`\nin one or two instructions (`hlp_inline_alloc_layout`): on Linux it is\n`thread pointer + offset` -- the struct is in static TLS, so the offset\nis the same on every thread, checked once by comparing two threads; on\nmacOS/aarch64 its address is published into a pthread TSD slot at mutator\nregistration and compiled code indexes the slot from `TPIDRRO_EL0`,\nchecked once against `pthread_getspecific`. `Tlab` is `repr(C)` so the\nfield offsets are an ABI. The emitted sequence is the allocator's own:\nno object crosses a line, the size in quanta goes into the objects map\nbefore the cursor moves, the type header is the first word, and the\nruntime call is the slow path (no region, region full, unregistered\nthread, TSD slot empty). The type's proto is resolved at compile time,\nsince the inlined path never reaches the runtime's lazy resolution.\nJIT only: an AOT binary has its own TLS layout, so the offset cannot be\nbaked at compile time; LLVM's own TLS relocations against an exported\nthread-local would be the AOT route.\n\n`ASH_INLINE_ALLOC=0` keeps every allocation in the runtime; GC stress\nalready disables the region and with it this path.","files":null}]}